re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x23d8-0x2440) + thread the engine 4937 c694 call's dropped bx=0x7aa4 descriptor
arg.  Clears the patch-293 frontier: the 459a mission paint pass now runs 4937's c694 cockpit-panel blit
crash-free instead of SIGSEGV-ing at m_mga_FUN_0000_23d8.

ORACLE VERDICT (decisive -- settles the recurring "0x7aa4 viewport geometry all-zero" question).  Ran the
instrumented DOSBox on the genuine BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186) AZER1 mission path
(tools/oracle/trace_activate.sh, engine guest-phys load base 0x11190 located by finding fist_dat_image.bin
content at phys 0x11590; DGROUP asm-offset Z -> phys 0x11190+0x1c000+Z).  At the settled AZER1 cockpit frame
(frame.png = full terrain + HUD + radar):
  - DGROUP:0x7aa4 (DST desc, phys 0x34c34) = 28 bytes ALL ZERO; DGROUP:0x7ac0 (SRC, 0x34c50) = ALL ZERO.
  - DAT_2000_3aa2 gate (phys 0x34c32) = 0 -> the 60d9 SRC->DST viewport-geometry copier NEVER RAN.
  - d548 (0x1548, phys 0x2e6d8) = 0x81 -> 4937's blit gate (bit7 set, low==1) IS satisfied -> the ORIGINAL
    reaches the c694 blit WITH the empty descriptor.
  - the fb-writer histogram shows 23d8's own rep-movs (eip 0x2422/0x2427/0x242b) DO write 0xA000 -> the
    original runs 23d8 crash-free on the empty descriptor.
VERDICT: the descriptor is GENUINELY EMPTY (no upstream populator exists -- 3aa2 gate never fires in either
target).  The original does not crash because 23d8 is a segmented real-mode blitter: word[desc]=0 -> BP=0 ->
DS=seg 0 (real-mode IVT, all valid memory) -> the RLE control stream terminates; ES=0xA000 writes are valid
VGA.  So the fix is NOT an upstream populator -- it is a FAITHFUL 23d8 that handles the empty descriptor
exactly as the original (simulated both seg-0 decodes: original terminates in 193 steps, the port's g_mem
low-code seg-0 terminates in 99 steps -- both crash-free, di/si/bx stay in g_mem bounds via 16-bit wrap).

THE BUG (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin).  FUN_0000_23d8 (0x23d8-0x2440):
  23e5 mov es,0xa000 ; 23ea xor di,di ; 23ec mov bp,[bx] (ctrl seg) ; 23f0 mov dx,[0x156c] (pixel seg)
  23f4 mov bx,[bx+0x1a] (pixel off) ; 23f7 mov ds,bp ; then an RLE decode with rep movsw/movsb copying
  pixel_seg:SI -> ES:DI, control words lods'd from ctrl_seg:SI.
Ghidra rendered the whole thing with HOST pointers: puVar11 (control cursor) inits to 0 with the BP segment
base DROPPED and mis-typed uint* (4-byte read/stride vs the asm's 2-byte lods); puVar12 (dest) inits to 0
with ES=0xA000 dropped; puVar10 (pixel src) = param_2[0xd] as a host pointer with the DX segment base
dropped -> NULL/host-ptr derefs -> SIGSEGV.  The decode-COUNT logic (words=(a>>2)*2+((a>>1)&1), bytes=a&1
where a=ctrlword>>1) was correct; only the three segment bases + the control-cursor width were wrong.

FIX.
 (1) fist_mga.c FUN_0000_23d8: exact asm translation with 16-bit registers (uint16 wrap) and g_mem-relative
     segment bases -- ctrl=g_mem+(word[desc]<<4), pix=g_mem+((uint16)_DAT_1000_d56c<<4), fb=g_mem+0xA0000;
     the descriptor is a DGROUP near offset (both callers pass a value) -> desc=g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)param_2.
     2e3f (clip setup, pure-DGROUP, safe on the zero descriptor) + 2e8b (teardown) unchanged.
 (2) fist.c FUN_0000_4937: `(*c694)(0xf69)` -> `(*c694)(0,0x7aa4)` -- asm 0x498e sets bx=0x7aa4 (param_2);
     ax (param_1) is unused by 23d8, pass 0.

